      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`/v1/models` returns `max_model_len` for the base model but `null` for every LoRA adapter. An adapter runs on the base model with the same context length, so a client that reads `max_model_len` from the card of the model it calls (to size prompts or `max_tokens`) gets nothing for adapters. This PR sets the adapter cards' `max_model_len` to the base model's value.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Each LoRA card in `/v1/models` now has the same `max_model_len` as the base model card.\n- The other card fields are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- New test `test_show_available_models_lora_card_has_max_model_len` in `tests/entrypoints/serve/lora/test_serving_models.py` registers one adapter at startup (`lora_modules`) and loads one at runtime, then checks `max_model_len` on all three cards. On main both adapter cards have `None`.\n- `pytest tests/entrypoints/serve/lora/test_serving_models.py`: 12 passed on this branch; on main the new test fails and the other 11 pass.\n- `pre-commit run --files` on the changed files passes.\n\n## Details\n\n`OpenAIModelRegistry.show_available_models()` builds the base cards with `max_model_len=self.model_config.max_model_len`, and `OpenAIServingModels.show_available_models()` then appends the LoRA cards without it. The fix passes the same value to every card built from `lora_requests`, which holds startup, runtime and resolver-loaded adapters alike.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
